:Namespace Othello
⍝ Othello in Dyalog APL: a port of the Rust engine in ~/work/crust/othello (see CLAUDE.md).
    ⎕IO←0

⍝ ─── Board and moves: a board is 2 64⍴ boolean [me;opp], square i = 8⊥rank file, a1 = 0
    Bd←{⍉(⍳64)∘.∊⍺ ⍵} ⍝ board from my squares ⍺ and opponent squares ⍵
    Sides←0 1(⌷⍤0 2)¨⊂ ⍝ boards (…,2,64) → mine theirs, each (…,64)
    S←{(mask⍴⍨⍴⍵)∧(rot⍴⍨¯1↓⍴⍵)⌽⍵} ⍝ shift each (…,8,64) direction row one step; edges fall off
    Run←{O←8 64∘⍴⍤1⊢⍺ ⋄ {⍵∨O∧S ⍵}⍣≡O∧S 8 64∘⍴⍤1⊢⍵} ⍝ (…,8,64): per direction, contiguous discs ⍺ reached from ⍵
    Moves←{m o←Sides ⍵ ⋄ (~m∨o)∧∨⌿⍤2⊢S o Run m} ⍝ legal moves for each board (…,2,64)
    Flips←{m o←Sides ⍵ ⋄ x←o Run ⍺∘.=⍳64 ⋄ ∨⌿⍤2⊢x∧⍤1 0∨/(8 64∘⍴⍤1⊢m)∧S x} ⍝ discs flipped by playing squares ⍺ on boards ⍵
    Play←{f←⍺ Flips ⍵ ⋄ ⊖⍤2⊢⍵≠(f∨⍺∘.=⍳64),[¯0.5]⍤1⊢f} ⍝ play squares ⍺ on boards ⍵; results are from the opponent's view
    Terminal←{~∨/⍵∨⍥Moves⊖⍤2⊢⍵} ⍝ neither side can move, per board
    Score←{d+(×d)×64-+/c⊣d←-/c←+/⍵} ⍝ WTHOR disc difference: empties go to the winner
    Perft←{ ⍝ leaf count to depth ⍺ from board(s) ⍵, a ply at a time; a pass is a ply, a terminal node counts 1
        b←⍵⍴⍨¯3↑1,⍴⍵
        ⍺=0:≢b
        m←Moves b
        ⍺=1:+/1⌈+/m
        i s←↓0 64⊤⍸,m
        p←⊖⍤2⊢b⌿⍨~∨/m
        t←~∨/Moves p
        (+/t)+(⍺-1)∇(s Play b[i;;])⍪p⌿⍨~t
    }
    Key←{zobrist+.×⍨⍵⍴⍨128,⍨¯2↓⍴⍵} ⍝ hash of each board: sum of random 45-bit numbers over its 128 bits, exact below 2*53

⍝ ─── Squares, pictures, games and agents
    Name←{r f←8 8⊤⍵ ⋄ 'abcdefgh'[f],⎕D[1+r]} ⍝ square ⍵ as 'd3'
    Sq←{2≠≢⍵:¯1 ⋄ 8∊i←'abcdefgh' '12345678'⍳¨⍵:¯1 ⋄ 8⊥⌽i} ⍝ square from 'd3'; ¯1 if malformed
    Show←{ ⍝ picture of game ⍵ ≡ colour board (colour 0: Black to move), in the oracle's format
        c b←⍵ ⋄ k←⊖⍣c⊢b
        g←'87654321',⊖8 8⍴'.XO'[1 2+.×k]
        ↑(⊂' abcdefgh'),(↓g),⊂(c⊃'Black' 'White'),' to move. Black ',(⍕+/k[0;]),', White ',(⍕+/k[1;]),', legal:',∊' ',¨Name¨⍸Moves b
    }
    Parse←{c←'W'=⊃⍵[9;] ⋄ c(⊖⍣c⊢'XO'∘.=,⊖⍵[1+⍳8;1+⍳8])} ⍝ game from its picture; inverse of Show
    Game←{ ⍝ agent ⍺⍺ moves now, ⍵⍵ next; ⍵ is (colour board); an agent maps a game to a square, or ¯1 to stop
        c b←⍵
        Terminal b:⍵
        ~∨/Moves b:(⍵⍵ ∇∇ ⍺⍺)(~c)(⊖b)
        s←⍺⍺ ⍵
        s<0:⍵
        s∊⍸Moves b:(⍵⍵ ∇∇ ⍺⍺)(~c)(s Play b)
        'illegal move'⎕SIGNAL 11
    }
    Rnd←{s←⍸Moves 1⊃⍵ ⋄ s[?≢s]} ⍝ agent: random legal move
    Human←{⎕←Show ⍵ ⋄ x←⎕C(' '≠x)/x←⍞ ⋄ x≡,'q':¯1 ⋄ s←Sq x ⋄ s∊⍸Moves 1⊃⍵:s ⋄ ⎕←'Illegal move' ⋄ ∇⍵} ⍝ agent: ask at the keyboard; q quits
    Result←{c b←⍵ ⋄ (¯1*c)×Score b} ⍝ Black's WTHOR margin of finished game ⍵

⍝ ─── Evaluation and search (scores in centidiscs)
    Div←(××⌊⍤|)÷ ⍝ integer division truncating toward zero, like Rust
    Eval←{ ⍝ oracle evaluate in centidiscs (±6400) for each board (…,2,64): table, mobility, frontier, corner risk, blended by phase
        ⍝ ⍺ (optional): move counts of the side to move and of the opponent
        ⍺←+/∘Moves¨⍵(⊖⍤2⊢⍵) ⋄ a t←⍺
        m o←Sides ⍵ ⋄ e←~m∨o ⋄ d←m-o
        p←⌊48÷⍨1000×60-12⌈60⌊+/e
        B←{⍵[0]+1000 Div⍨p×-/⌽⍵}
        v←d+.×,weights
        v+←1000 Div⍨(B 500 800)×(a+t+1)Div⍨1000×a-t
        v-←(B 10 4)×+/d×∨⌿⍤2⊢S 8 64∘⍴⍤1⊢e
        v-←1000 Div⍨(B 1000 700)×+/(e+.×corners)×d+.×risk
        6400⌊¯6400⌈v
    }
    Leaf←{ ⍝ (E Leaf) depth-0 value under evaluator E of each board in stack ⍵, as Search would give it: exact if finished, opponent's Eval negated after a forced pass
        a t←+/∘Moves¨⍵(⊖⍤2⊢⍵)
        v←(a t)⍺⍺ ⍵
        ~0∊a:v
        i←⍸(a=0)∧t>0 ⋄ v[i]←-(t[i])(a[i])⍺⍺⊖⍤2⊢⍵[i;;]
        i←⍸0=a+t ⋄ v[i]←100×Score ⍵[i;;]
        v
    }
    Wide←{⍵,inf×¯1 1} ⍝ depth ⍵ with the full alpha-beta window
    New←{ ⍝ empty transposition table with 2*⍵ slots, plus the search's limits, counters and configuration
        s←2*⍵
        (size:s ⋄ key:s⍴¯1 ⋄ val:s⍴0 ⋄ dep:s⍴¯1 ⋄ bnd:s⍴0 ⋄ mv:s⍴¯1   ⍝ slots; per slot key (¯1 empty), value, depth, bound (0 exact 1 lower 2 upper), move
         dl:⌊/⍬ ⋄ mx:0 ⋄ n:0                             ⍝ deadline (⎕AI[2] ms), node limit (0 none), nodes so far
         ord:1 ⋄ tt:1 ⋄ base:0)                          ⍝ oracle SearchConfig: move ordering, table use, frozen baseline Eval2
    }
    Search←{ ⍝ ⍺ ≡ depth alpha beta [table]; fail-soft negamax of board ⍵ → value, best square (¯1 if none chosen)
        d a z←3↑⍺ ⋄ T←3{⍺=≢⍵:(n:0) ⋄ ⍺⊃⍵}⍺                        ⍝ no table: a namespace that only counts nodes
        tt ord base dl mx←T⎕VGET('tt' 0)('ord' 1)('base' 0)('dl'(⌊/⍬))('mx' 0)
        (⎕AI[2]≥dl)∨(mx>0)∧T.n≥mx:⎕SIGNAL 999                      ⍝ out of time or nodes: abandon (nothing stored)
        T.n+←1
        Ev←{⍺←⊢ ⋄ base:⍺ Eval2 ⍵ ⋄ ⍺ Eval ⍵}
        s←⍸Moves ⍵
        0=≢s:{∨/Moves⊖⍵:¯1,⍨-⊃(T,⍨d,-z a)Search⊖⍵ ⋄ ¯1,⍨100×Score ⍵}⍵
        d=0:¯1,⍨Ev ⍵
        k i e←{~tt:0 0 0 ⋄ k←Key ⍵ ⋄ i←T.size|k ⋄ k i(T.key[i]=k)}⍵
        {~e:0 ⋄ T.dep[i]≠d:0 ⋄ f x←T.bnd[i],T.val[i] ⋄ (f=⍳3)∨.∧1,(z≤x),x≤a}0:T.val[i],T.mv[i]
        h←{~e:¯1 ⋄ T.dep[i]≥d:T.mv[i] ⋄ ¯1}0
        c←s Play(≢s)2 64⍴⍵
        v←-Ev Leaf c ⋄ T.n+←≢c                                     ⍝ nodes: Search calls plus boards scored
        o←{ord:⍵ ⋄ ⍳≢s}⍒v ⋄ o←(o/⍨s[o]=h),o/⍨s[o]≠h  ⍝ table move first, then static value
        L←{i b m a←⍵ ⋄ i=≢o:b m ⋄ x←-⊃(T,⍨(d-1),-z a)Search c[o[i];;] ⋄ b m←(x>b)⊃(b m)(x,s[o[i]]) ⋄ a⌈←x ⋄ a≥z:b m ⋄ ∇(i+1)b m a}
        r←{d=1:(⌈/v),s[⊃⍒v] ⋄ L 0(-inf)¯1 a}0
        ~tt:r
        T.key[i]←k ⋄ T.val[i]←⊃r ⋄ T.dep[i]←d ⋄ T.mv[i]←1⊃r
        w←⊃r ⋄ T.bnd[i]←(d>1)×(z≤w)+2×w≤a
        r
    }
    Think←{ ⍝ ⍺ ≡ ms [depth [nodes [threshold]]]: search board ⍵ (with a legal move) within limits
        ⍝ → square value depth nodes status solved; status 0 complete, 1 partial (a limit stopped later work),
        ⍝   2 fallback (nothing completed: first legal move, static value). Depth 0 for an exact solve.
        ⍝ At most threshold (default 12: 12-empty solves finish within 5 s here, 14-empty mostly do not) empties: root-only solve, win/draw/loss first, then the exact margin.
        ⍝ Otherwise iterative deepening, stopping at depth ≥ empties (exact: passes cost no depth).
        ⍝ A search to depth ≥ empties sees only finished games, so solving is Search with depth = empties.
        ms n x th←4↑⍺,(≢⍺)↓0 64 0 12
        T←(New 20)⎕VSET('dl'(⎕AI[2]+ms))('mx'x) ⋄ b←⍵ ⋄ e←+/~∨⌿b
        f←(⊃⍸Moves b)(Eval b)0 0 2 0
        e≤th:{
            w←{999::f ⋄ v s←(e,¯1 1,T)Search b ⋄ s v 0 T.n 1 0}0
            2=4⊃w:w
            a z←¯1 1×1⌈inf×(1⊃w)×¯1 1  ⍝ win: ¯1 inf, loss: -inf 1, draw: ¯1 1
            999::w ⋄ v s←(e,a,z,T)Search b ⋄ s v 0 T.n 0 1
        }0
        n⌊←e
        G←{d r←⍵ ⋄ d>n:r ⋄ 999::r ⋄ v s←(T,⍨Wide d)Search b ⋄ ∇(d+1)(s v d T.n(d<n)0)}
        G 1 f
    }
    AB←{1⊃(Wide ⍺⍺)Search 1⊃⍵} ⍝ agent: alpha-beta to depth ⍺⍺
    TH←{⊃⍺⍺ Think 1⊃⍵} ⍝ agent: iterative deepening within limits ⍺⍺ ≡ ms [depth [nodes]]

⍝ ─── Match harness: frozen baseline, agents, opening replay, pairs, statistics, opening splits
    Eval2←{⍺←0 ⋄ m o←Sides ⍵ ⋄ 6400⌊¯6400⌈(100×(+/m)-+/o)+(m-o)+.×,weights2} ⍝ frozen phase-2 baseline (oracle eval_phase2): discs×100 + table weights2; ⍺ (move counts) ignored
    RA←{b←1⊃⍵ ⋄ s←⍸Moves b ⋄ ⎕RL←1+2147483646|⍺⍺+Key b ⋄ s[?≢s]} ⍝ agent (seed RA): random move, reproducible from seed and position
    Greedy←{b←1⊃⍵ ⋄ s←⍸Moves b ⋄ s[⊃⍒+/(s Play(≢s)2 64⍴b)[;1;]]} ⍝ agent: most discs after the move, lowest square on ties
    P2←{T←(New 16)⎕VSET⊂'base' 1 ⋄ 1⊃(T,⍨Wide ⍺⍺)Search 1⊃⍵} ⍝ agent (d P2): current search to depth d with the frozen Eval2, fresh table each move
    Replay←{ ⍝ game after opening squares ⍵ from game ⍺ (default: start, Black to move); colour toggles on placements and passes
        ⍺←0 start ⋄ 0=≢⍵:⍺ ⋄ c b←⍺
        Terminal b:'opening runs past the end of the game'⎕SIGNAL 11
        ~∨/Moves b:((~c)(⊖b))∇⍵
        (⊃⍵)∊⍸Moves b:((~c)((⊃⍵)Play b))∇1↓⍵
        'illegal opening move'⎕SIGNAL 11
    }
    Done←{Terminal 1⊃⍵:⍵ ⋄ 'agent stopped with legal moves'⎕SIGNAL 11} ⍝ a match game must be played to the end
    Duel←{ ⍝ agent ⍺⍺ plays Black, ⍵⍵ White, from game ⍵ → finished game
        ⊃⍵:Done(⍵⍵ Game ⍺⍺)⍵
        Done(⍺⍺ Game ⍵⍵)⍵
    }
    Pts←{0.5×1+×Result ⍵} ⍝ Black's points for finished game ⍵: win 1, draw ½, loss 0
    Pair←{g←Replay ⍵ ⋄ (Pts(⍺⍺ Duel ⍵⍵)g),1-Pts(⍵⍵ Duel ⍺⍺)g} ⍝ A ≡ ⍺⍺'s points from opening ⍵ as Black, then as White
    Match←{↑(⍺⍺ Pair ⍵⍵)¨↓⍵} ⍝ agents ⍺⍺ (A) and ⍵⍵ (B) over openings ⍵ (one per row) → per pair: A's points in its two games
    Boot←{ ⍝ seed ⍺; pair scores ⍵ → mean low high informative (oracle stats policy); ⍬ if no pairs
        n←≢⍵ ⋄ n=0:⍬
        m←(+/⍵)÷n ⋄ v←(+/(⍵-m)*2)÷n
        (n<10)∨v=0:m,(0⌈m-h),(1⌊m+h←((⍟40)÷2×n)*0.5),0  ⍝ Hoeffding: uninformative
        ⎕RL←⍺ ⋄ r←{⍵[⍋⍵]}(+/⍵[?10000 n⍴n])÷n
        m,r[⌊0.5+9999×0.025 0.975],1  ⍝ percentile pair bootstrap, 10 000 resamples
    }
    Elo←{400×10⍟⍵÷1-⍵} ⍝ rating difference for expected score ⍵
    Report←{ ⍝ seed ⍺; Match result ⍵ → text: pairs, W/D/L, mean pair score with interval, Elo range when both ends are inside (0,1)
        p←(+/⍵)÷2 ⋄ w d l←+/1 0.5 0∘.=,⍵ ⋄ b←⍺ Boot p
        0=≢b:'insufficient data'
        m lo hi i←b ⋄ F←{1⍕⍵} ⋄ G←{3⍕⍵}
        e←{(lo>0)∧hi<1:'  Elo [',(F Elo lo),',',(F Elo hi),']' ⋄ ''}0
        'pairs ',(⍕≢p),'  W/D/L ',(⍕w),'/',(⍕d),'/',(⍕l),'  score ',(G m),' [',(G lo),',',(G hi),'] ',(i⊃'uninformative' 'bootstrap'),e
    }
    Tr←{s←⍴⍵ ⋄ s⍴(⌽∘⍉⍣(4|⍺))∘(⍉⍣(⍺≥4))⍤2⊢((¯1↓s),8 8)⍴⍵} ⍝ D4 element ⍺∊⍳8 applied to board or 64-vector ⍵
    Canon←{b←⍵ ⋄ ⌊/{Key ⍵ Tr b}¨⍳8} ⍝ canonical D4 key of board ⍵: least key over its 8 symmetries
    Splits←{ ⍝ opening sets ⍵ (one matrix each) → (per set: openings, duplicate lines, plies, ply-4 groups, first 20 in distinct groups) (groups shared by two sets)
        G←{Canon 1⊃Replay 4↑⍵} ⋄ gk←{G¨↓⍵}¨⍵
        s←↑{(≢⍵),((≢⍵)-≢∪↓⍵),(⊃⌽⍴⍵)}¨⍵
        (s,(≢¨∪¨gk),⍪{20=≢∪20↑⍵}¨gk)(+/,(∘.<⍨⍳≢gk)×∘.{≢⍺∩⍵}⍨∪¨gk)
    }

⍝ ─── Tests: RunTests 0 → names of failing Test* functions; Slow* by hand. Naive reference and helpers first
    RunTests←{t←{⍵/⍨(⊂'Test')≡¨4↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3 ⋄ t/⍨~{⍎⍵,' 0'}¨t} ⍝ names of failing tests
    NRay←{c←⍺∘+¨⍵∘×¨1+⍳7 ⋄ 8⊥¨c/⍨∧\{∧/(⍵≥0)∧⍵<8}¨c} ⍝ squares walked from (rank file) ⍺ in direction ⍵
    NFlips←{ ⍝ naive Flips: walk coordinates from square ⍺ on board ⍵
        v←-⌿⍵ ⋄ p←8 8⊤⍺
        (⍳64)∊∊{r←p NRay ⍵ ⋄ w←v[r] ⋄ n←+/∧\w=¯1 ⋄ n=≢w:⍬ ⋄ (1=w[n])/n↑r}¨(,∘.,⍨¯1 0 1)~⊂0 0
    }
    NMoves←{e←⍸~∨⌿⍵ ⋄ (⍳64)∊e/⍨∨/¨e NFlips¨⊂⍵} ⍝ naive Moves
    NPlay←{f←⍺ NFlips ⍵ ⋄ (⍸⍵[1;]>f)Bd ⍺,⍸⍵[0;]∨f} ⍝ naive Play, built from square lists
    Playout←{Terminal ⍵:,⊂⍵ ⋄ r←⍺ ⋄ s←⍸Moves ⍵ ⋄ (⊂⍵),(1↓r)∇{0=≢s:⊖⍵ ⋄ s[⌊(≢s)×⊃r]Play ⍵}⍵} ⍝ boards of a game from ⍵, moves chosen by fractions ⍺
    Positions←{⎕RL←⍺ ⋄ ⊃,/(↓?(⍵,70)⍴0)Playout¨⊂start} ⍝ boards from ⍵ random games with seed ⍺ (⎕RL set here is not seen by called dfns, so draw here)
    MM←{ ⍝ plain minimax to depth ⍺, one board at a time, no batching or pruning
        s←⍸Moves ⍵
        0=≢s:⍺{∨/Moves⊖⍵:-⍺ MM⊖⍵ ⋄ 100×Score ⍵}⍵
        ⍺=0:Eval ⍵
        ⌈/-(⍺-1)MM¨s Play¨⊂⍵
    }
    Diff←{∧/{b←⍵ ⋄ ((Moves b)≡NMoves b)∧∧/{(⍵ Play b)≡⍵ NPlay b}¨⍸NMoves b}¨⍵} ⍝ production ≡ naive on boards ⍵
    Corp←{⊂[1 2]'1'=(≢c)2 64⍴↑c←Data'Corpus'} ⍝ corpus boards: 0–11 midgame (28–40 empties), 12–19 late (12–16), 20–25 with a move that forces a pass
    BenchPos←{⊃,/{((31+⍵)Positions 1)[20 30]}¨⍳3} ⍝ six fixed midgame positions
    Bench←{ ⍝ depths ⍵ → per depth: depth, total ms over BenchPos, sum of values (to spot behaviour changes)
        p←BenchPos 0
        ↑{d←⍵ ⋄ t←⎕AI[2] ⋄ v←{⊃(Wide d)Search ⍵}¨p ⋄ d(⎕AI[2]-t)(+/v)}¨⍵
    }
    BenchID←{ ⍝ depths ⍵ → per depth: depth, total ms over BenchPos for iterative deepening to that depth, sum of values
        p←BenchPos 0
        ↑{d←⍵ ⋄ t←⎕AI[2] ⋄ v←{1⊃(⌊/⍬)d 0 0 Think ⍵}¨p ⋄ d(⎕AI[2]-t)(+/v)}¨⍵
    }
    Nodes←{ ⍝ ⍺ ≡ ordering table (0/1 switches); ⍵ depth → nodes and ms for iterative deepening to ⍵ over the midgame corpus
        o u←⍺ ⋄ d←⍵ ⋄ t←⎕AI[2]
        n←+/{T←(New 20)⎕VSET('ord'o)('tt'u) ⋄ b←⍵ ⋄ z←{(T,⍨Wide ⍵)Search b}¨1+⍳d ⋄ T.n}¨12↑Corp 0
        n(⎕AI[2]-t)
    }
    SlowDiff←{Diff 1729 Positions 100}
    SlowEndBench←{ ⍝ empties ⍵ → per count: positions, solved within 5 s, median, p90, max ms (10 positions each, seed 41)
        g←{⍵/⍨{∨/Moves ⍵}¨⍵}41 Positions 30
        ↑{e←⍵ ⋄ p←10↑g/⍨e={+/~∨⌿⍵}¨g
            r←{t←⎕AI[2] ⋄ x←5000 64 0 14 Think ⍵ ⋄ (5⊃x),⎕AI[2]-t}¨p
            s←{⍵[⍋⍵]}1⊃¨r ⋄ e(≢p)(+/⊃¨r),s[⌊0.5+(¯1+≢s)×0.5 0.9 1]}¨⍵
    }
    SlowGame←{ ⍝ Phase 6 gate: a full game, engine at 5 s per move (solver from 12 empties) vs seeded random → longest move ms, engine's moves, final Black margin
        t←⍬ ⋄ r←?70⍴0
        E←{s←⎕AI[2] ⋄ m←⊃5000 Think 1⊃⍵ ⋄ t,←⎕AI[2]-s ⋄ m}
        R←{s←⍸Moves 1⊃⍵ ⋄ s[⌊(≢s)×r[+/,1⊃⍵]]}
        g←(E Game R)0 start
        (⌈/t)(≢t)(Result g)
    }
    SlowGate←{ ⍝ oracle Phase 3 gate: phase2 vs greedy, 200 pairs, seed 1, reproducible with a valid interval → report, repeat identical
        o←200↑Data'OpenTune'
        m←((4 P2)Match Greedy)o
        (1 Report m)(m≡((4 P2)Match Greedy)o)
    }
    SlowPerft←{3005288 24571284≡9 10 Perft¨⊂start}
    SlowSolve←{ ⍝ oracle's known endgames (tests/search.rs solver_known_endgames): 12 and 11 empties → values ≡ ¯2200 1800, and ms each
        a←(0 4 8 10 11 16 17 18 19 22 24 28 29 30 31 32 37 38 39 43 45 46 50 51 52 54 59 60 61 62)Bd 5 7 12 13 14 20 21 25 26 27 33 34 35 36 40 41 42 44 48 49 53 57
        b←(12 18 19 23 27 30 31 38 39 40 41 45 48 49 50 53 54 55 56 57)Bd 1 2 3 4 5 6 9 10 11 13 14 17 20 21 22 24 25 26 28 29 33 34 35 36 37 42 43 44 51 52 60 62 63
